0..63 Comment "// Data arrows state constructors, operations, rules and cells."
64..140 Comment "// `IntOp` carries an operation that the integers of `data-base.gandr` lack,"
141..169 Comment "// so it takes another name."
170..172 Comment "//"
173..213 Comment "// A single shaft defines a constructor."
214..253 Comment "// A double shaft defines an operation."
254..295 Comment "// A left head makes an arrow invertible."
296..298 Comment "//"
299..327 Comment "// Constructors build terms."
328..353 Comment "// Operations form terms."
354..414 Comment "// A directed rule computes its left side to its right side."
415..489 Comment "// An invertible rule spells one term two ways, and the term order chooses"
490..507 Comment "// its direction."
508..541 Comment "// Cells add paths between terms."
542..544 Comment "//"
545..624 Comment "// - see: `pathological/identity/directed-cell.gandr` — the checker refuses a"
625..651 Comment "//   directed cell by name"
653..715 Comment "/// `IntOp` has two constructors, two rules and one operation."
